{
  "info": {
    "name": "AWTY — Are We There Yet?",
    "_postman_id": "awty-collection-v1",
    "description": "REST and WebSocket endpoints for the AWTY task processing API.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "taskId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Populated automatically by the 'Create Task' post-script."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Tasks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('taskId', json.id);",
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Returns pending task', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('pending');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"duration\": 10\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks"]
            },
            "description": "Enqueues a new task. Returns immediately with id + 'pending' status. The `duration` field controls how many seconds the simulated task runs (1–300)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Task — Validation Error",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Returns error body', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('error');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"duration\": -5\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks"]
            },
            "description": "Sends an invalid duration to verify Zod validation rejects it with HTTP 400."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Valid task shape', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(['pending','processing','completed','failed']).to.include(json.status);",
                  "  pm.expect(json.progress).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "{{taskId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Polls the current persisted state of a task. Run 'Create Task' first so {{taskId}} is set."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Task — Not Found",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tasks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["tasks", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies a non-existent task ID returns HTTP 404."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Socket.IO — Subscribe (docs)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": {
          "raw": "http://localhost:3000",
          "protocol": "http",
          "host": ["localhost"],
          "port": "3000"
        },
        "description": "Socket.IO endpoint. Use the socket.io-client library or a tool like Firecamp / Insomnia for native Socket.IO support.\n\n**Connect:**\n```js\nimport { io } from 'socket.io-client';\nconst socket = io('http://localhost:3000');\n```\n\n**Subscribe to a task:**\n```js\nsocket.emit('subscribe', { taskId: '<uuid from Create Task>' });\n```\n\n**Listen for events:**\n```js\nsocket.on('progress',  ({ taskId, progress }) => console.log(progress));\nsocket.on('completed', ({ taskId }) => console.log('done'));\nsocket.on('failed',    ({ taskId }) => console.log('failed'));\n```\n\nOn subscription the server immediately replays the latest persisted state for reconnection recovery."
      }
    }
  ]
}
